# Topic: scripts run, and constants fold, in the host's float mode
#
# What it does: lua_setfloatmode gives a VM the float mode its interpreter runs in: FLUSH (x86's SSE flush-to-zero with
# denormals-are-zero off: a subnormal result is zero, a subnormal operand is still read as itself), KEEP (IEEE 754's gradual
# underflow) or THREAD (the default: the calling thread's mode as it is). The VM's outermost entry from C (a call, a resume, a
# Luau metamethod's call) applies it and puts the caller's back when it returns; a nested entry only counts itself (reading the
# mode register waits for the float operations in flight, and a resume re-enters the interpreter for every yieldable pcall).
# luaD_rawrunprotected resets the count and the mode once an error is caught (the VM is built without unwind semantics on MSVC,
# so a destructor does not run while an error unwinds its frame, and on Windows a restore inside the catch block is undone by the
# unwind that follows it); luau_codegen_compile
# folds constants in the VM's mode; luau_compile folds them in the flushing mode when the options list
# LUAU_COMPILE_FLOATMODE_FLUSH among the mutable globals (the options' C layout is the binding's to fill). x86-64 only: elsewhere
# no mode flushes results alone, and every mode is the thread's (Luau/FloatMode.h).
#
# Why upstream lacks it: upstream leaves the float environment to its host. Roblox's engine runs scripts with flush-to-zero on
# and denormals-are-zero off, except in a client's render step, and folds constants in that mode (measured in Studio 0.747 on a
# client, a server and in edit mode: tools/parity/probes/float_flush.luau). The mode is set here, around the interpreter and the
# compilers, because a host in Rust may not change it: its compiler assumes the default float environment, so no host code runs
# in the mode but the C functions a script calls, as an engine's own code runs in its scripts' mode.

